    <Comments>
      <Comment>A demo of the Glide (Gxx) command</Comment>
      <Comment/>
      <Comment>A phrase contains three note columns, with various glide commands located in the master effect-column.</Comment>
      <Comment/>
      <Comment>-- Things to notice: </Comment>
      <Comment/>
      <Comment>* G00 means 'repeat with same value as above' - saves us from having to write G40, G80 etc. more than once</Comment>
      <Comment/>
      <Comment>* Entering a glide command avoids retriggering the sample. Instead, it remains looped / sustained. </Comment>
      <Comment>In this phrase - since glide is used on every note - the attack stage is only heard once, when the phrase is first triggered</Comment>
    </Comments>
